      "text": "{\"pair_id\": \"Kemsit|860747\", \"verdict\": \"different_name\", \"reasoning\": \"The transliteration Kwms reads as the signs k, w, m, s. In Kemsit, k is matched by K and w may be left out, since a modern spelling can omit w. The e is an extra vowel letter that stands for no sign. m is matched by m and s by s. After the s, record 1 still has 'i' and 't'. The i could be an extra vowel letter, but the final t is a consonant that matches no sign of Kwms, which ends in s. The permitted omission of a final feminine t applies only when record 1 leaves out a t that the transliteration has. It does not allow record 1 to add one. Because record 1 has a leftover consonant, the two are different names.\"}"
